1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:06,000
So, the task is to build a voltage inverter rated 800 volts, 2 amps.

2
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:13,420
The load will be 300 watt lamps, 4 of them connected in series, and bundled in parallel as 3 strings.

3
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,880
3 bundles of 4 lamps in parallel.

4
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:21,800
For lamps per bundle to distribute the 800 volts as 200 volts per lamp.

5
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:32,140
So, we have a ferrite step-up transformer, we have a half-bridge inverter, this is the control board, the mains rectifier, and we'll be watching the consumption.

6
00:00:36,810 --> 00:00:38,050
So, we start it up.

7
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,780
We start the logic.

8
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:48,240
Off we go.

9
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:51,740
That's how this thing lights up.

10
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:58,640
Our consumption is 7.5 amps at 220 volts, AC ammeter.

11
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,950
Shutting it off, or the strip will burn out.

